\(y_1 = e^x \implies y_1'' = e^x \implies e^x - e^x = 0\), y \(y_2 = e^{-x} \implies y_2'' = e^{-x} \implies e^{-x} - e^{-x} = 0\). Ambos satisfacen la EDO. <br>
Calculamos el Wronskiano:
